From 92ba7813c0f8bb01ccf6d46aaeea2e37c663939e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:05:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Texture filtering: DuckStation's full set (xBR, Scale2x,
 Scale3x, MMPX, MMPX Enhanced, MMPX Advanced), edge blending, FMV chroma
 smoothing

The textured fragment shader is now one program per filter mode
(PSX_TEXFILTER at the top of the source, built on first use, nearest
always present for the per-batch 2D case), so a mode's code is the only
code that program carries. Modes 5..10 are DuckStation's shader blocks
lifted verbatim by tools/port_duckstation_texfilters.py into
gpu_gl_texfilters.h (three edits: the xBR I.w typo, MMPX's split #define,
0u literals for GLSL 3.30) behind a small HLSL-name compat layer; their
own cutout rule (coverage < 0.5 dropped) applies.

[video] texture_edge_blending: DuckStation's edge blending - filtered
cutout coverage multiplies the colour and 1-coverage keeps the
destination through the dual-source factor every opaque texel pass now
draws with (identical output for fully covered pixels), coverage below
one half dropped. [video] fmv_chroma_smoothing: DuckStation's 24-bit
chroma smoothing on the CPU FMV frame before upload (same matrices,
same even-aligned 2x2 block bilinear; verified against a port of the
shader to 1 LSB). Shader compiles refresh the starvation watchdog. The
pgxp debug command takes edge_blend / fmv_chroma live.
